WEBVTT

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:19.910
So this projects an image of me?

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:21.600
That's right.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:24.410
Give us an introduction, Kenroku!

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:26.540
What? You already started?

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.170
Ahem.

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:33.430
I'm Sanada Kenroku, 
a lower member of the Sanada family.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:37.180
Don't know why, but I've come here 
to Japan in the future.

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:42.100
Originally I served my clan,

00:00:42.490 --> 00:00:44.640
but the moment I thought 
about leaving the clan

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:47.880
to live a quiet life with 
the woman I fell in love with,

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:51.630
a rotten magistrate forced himself on her.

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:54.880
I stormed his place 
to make him suffer a bit,

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:57.730
but I went overboard and killed him.

00:00:57.730 --> 00:01:01.370
So then I was exiled, spirited away,

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:03.450
and now I'm here.

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:06.950
You really loved her, didn't you?

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:15.990
Hah, don't ask such a stupid question.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:18.220
<i>Oddly enough...</i>

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:22.720
Kenroku!

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:29.230
<i>You kind of resemble Okuni.</i>

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:33.860
<b>Sanada 
 Kenroku</b>

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.540
<b>"The Third Man"</b>

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:21.470
Kenroku, are you okay?

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:27.220
Yeah. We've found our way 
into one hell of a place, though.

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:31.100
Still, it's no different 
than the battlefield.

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:35.230
Maybe slightly better, 
since we're not facing people.

00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:39.580
The camp's in ruins.

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:44.490
Looks like the remaining Gibia 
withdrew when morning came.

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:47.130
We're the only ones left now,

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:49.370
so we'll have to relocate somewhere else.

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:52.830
Tokyo has a high population density,

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:54.880
so why don't we head into the countryside?

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:58.730
The area around Nagano 
is surrounded by mountains,

00:03:58.730 --> 00:04:01.230
so there might be people 
who haven't turned into Gibia there,

00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:05.640
and up in the Niigata area we could
 board boats to mainland Asia.

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:09.270
That's it!

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:13.140
If I recall, there should be a Gibiate 
research facility there in Niigata, too.

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:15.100
<b>Tokyo</b>

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:16.690
All right, let's head for Niigata.

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:19.980
It's not densely populated and 
there are mountains along the way,

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:22.400
<b>Niigata</b>

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:21.920
so there might be fewer Gibia.

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:23.990
It's settled, then.

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:31.330
Maeda-san...

00:04:36.910 --> 00:04:37.920
Kathleen.

00:04:38.780 --> 00:04:39.910
Sensui!

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:43.440
Sensui-kun.

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:46.500
In order to develop a vaccine for Gibia,

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:50.170
we'll need more of the venom 
contained in their stingers.

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:53.320
Would you help us collect it?

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:57.530
We'd be asking you to cut down 
as many Gibia as possible.

00:04:58.180 --> 00:04:59.280
All right.

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:05.200
I want to retrieve our Gibia Virus 
samples before we depart.

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:08.760
If all goes well, we might be able 
to obtain a helicopter, too.

00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:10.480
Please come with me.

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:26.580
This is where we had 
a sturdy preservation room

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:28.980
to store the Gibia Virus samples.

00:05:29.530 --> 00:05:32.220
We managed to make it this far 
thanks to you, Sensui-kun.

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:35.230
There's a helicopter on the roof.

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:39.230
I just hope it hasn't 
been destroyed by Gibia.

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:55.700
Is everyone ready?

00:05:56.270 --> 00:05:58.790
From here on, the rooms are dark.

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:01.840
There's guaranteed to be 
Gibia hiding inside.

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:03.820
Sensui-kun.

00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:07.920
We'll be relying on you two,

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:11.560
so please keep us safe until 
we reach the preservation room.

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:29.530
It's all right, everyone.

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:32.710
There are no more signs of Gibia nearby.

00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:47.290
Looks like things are still safe here.

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:51.050
The electricity's still working inside.

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:55.060
You all gather up the food 
and things we'll need.

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:57.260
I'll go to the preservation room.

00:06:57.950 --> 00:06:59.560
You don't need to worry.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:03.480
Let's set a time to meet up on the roof.

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:06.610
Christ!

00:07:06.970 --> 00:07:09.570
Yoshinaga's a cold bastard.

00:07:09.980 --> 00:07:14.010
The Doctor is trying to develop a vaccine 
to save the entire world by himself.

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:16.830
That pressure is huge.

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:20.570
Well, a lot of scholars 
are like that anyway.

00:07:20.570 --> 00:07:22.580
Don't say that, Adam.

00:07:38.530 --> 00:07:41.100
It's so close to completion.

00:07:42.860 --> 00:07:44.260
Excuse me.

00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:46.800
Brian?

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:48.880
What's the matter?

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:52.970
Nothing. We just finished 
most of what we came here for.

00:07:54.110 --> 00:07:55.410
I see.

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:57.730
I'll head up shortly myself.

00:07:57.730 --> 00:07:58.850
Yes.

00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:03.210
What is it?

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:08.880
I'll head up later. You should 
return to everyone first.

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:10.880
Um!

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:14.260
Doctor! Will you be able 
to complete the vaccine?!

00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:16.510
Did something happen?

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:26.170
I've lost a lot of my men.

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:28.950
I don't want to lose any more people.

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:34.410
Once your vaccine is complete, 
we can save many others.

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:38.400
That's when my men's sacrifice 
will finally be worth it.

00:08:41.230 --> 00:08:42.280
I see.

00:08:42.280 --> 00:08:43.960
It's almost complete.

00:08:44.280 --> 00:08:49.730
Fortunately, we have powerful allies 
in Sensui-kun and Kenroku-kun now.

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:53.160
We should be able to collect 
many samples with their help.

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:55.180
Really?!

00:08:57.040 --> 00:08:59.940
Yes. We will complete it.

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:05.530
We will develop the vaccine 
to make Gibia human again.

00:09:11.420 --> 00:09:14.490
We've gathered just about 
everything we need.

00:09:16.050 --> 00:09:18.780
Why are you the only one 
empty-handed, Sensui?!

00:09:19.590 --> 00:09:23.460
Because we need him to be able to fight 
when and if something happens.

00:09:23.460 --> 00:09:27.750
That's right! Sensui's our bodyguard!

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:31.500
Are you saying you can't rely on me?

00:09:32.530 --> 00:09:35.260
Oh? Did I keep you all waiting long?

00:09:35.650 --> 00:09:38.910
No, we just got here.

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:45.270
Well, let's hop into the helicopter
 and fly to Niigata!

00:09:47.290 --> 00:09:49.140
What's wrong, Sensui?

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:52.700
I thought I felt something watching us.

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:56.280
What?! More Gibia?!

00:09:56.790 --> 00:09:59.900
No, I'm not sure what it is.

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:05.300
Huh? What's that?

00:10:07.200 --> 00:10:09.260
That's... a person?!

00:10:09.650 --> 00:10:12.330
No mistake! That's a person!

00:10:12.330 --> 00:10:13.300
Yoshinaga!

00:10:13.650 --> 00:10:15.310
There's a collapsed person out there!

00:10:16.890 --> 00:10:18.610
We have to go help them!

00:10:18.610 --> 00:10:21.240
But what if they turn into a Gibia?

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:26.390
We'll just have to cut him
 down if it comes to that.

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:33.820
However, with so few humans left alive, 
I'd like to save the ones we can.

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:35.990
Right!

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:42.230
Doctor, I'll pilot it!

00:10:43.070 --> 00:10:44.500
That's all right.

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:47.380
I've piloted a helicopter 
a few times before.

00:10:47.990 --> 00:10:49.190
Leave it to me.

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:00.780
Further right!

00:11:04.230 --> 00:11:07.270
I'll land in that space near the man!

00:11:19.850 --> 00:11:21.570
Wh-What?!

00:11:23.610 --> 00:11:25.340
What is that?!

00:11:38.890 --> 00:11:39.760
Hmm...

00:11:40.670 --> 00:11:46.850
That's a strange bird 
of paradise flying around.

00:11:54.070 --> 00:11:57.230
Is it being chased by a monster?!

00:11:58.170 --> 00:12:02.110
I thought you said Gibia
 didn't come out in bright places?!

00:12:03.310 --> 00:12:04.610
<i>That's...!</i>

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:11.120
Hey! Yoshinaga!

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:12.650
That's an abnormality!

00:12:12.650 --> 00:12:13.750
We're pulling out for now!

00:12:16.810 --> 00:12:17.980
Huh?

00:12:17.980 --> 00:12:20.000
We're leaving that person behind?

00:12:28.940 --> 00:12:31.140
Shit! It's got us!

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:39.400
Kenroku! What do you think you're doing?!

00:12:43.690 --> 00:12:45.480
Hold on, Kenroku!

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:47.660
Kenroku!

00:12:59.380 --> 00:13:00.420
Sensui!

00:13:02.570 --> 00:13:03.690
Kenroku!

00:13:09.870 --> 00:13:11.990
Scary!

00:13:11.990 --> 00:13:13.850
Not yet! Keep your wits about you!

00:13:14.240 --> 00:13:15.050
What?!

00:13:17.890 --> 00:13:20.360
Damn it! It didn't cut through!

00:13:24.460 --> 00:13:25.610
Shit, shit, shit!

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:31.890
Sensui!

00:13:37.950 --> 00:13:41.130
You're even more reckless than I am!

00:13:46.440 --> 00:13:49.550
Have those two lost their marbles?!

00:13:49.550 --> 00:13:50.890
We're at our limit!

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:52.080
Listen!

00:13:52.530 --> 00:13:54.890
Toss me to that Gibia!

00:13:55.180 --> 00:13:56.550
Are you sure?!

00:13:58.590 --> 00:14:00.930
Go, Sensui!

00:14:04.070 --> 00:14:05.900
I'll end it in one blow!

00:14:24.090 --> 00:14:25.460
Are you okay?!

00:14:25.460 --> 00:14:26.600
Kenroku!

00:14:26.830 --> 00:14:28.330
Sensui's in trouble!

00:14:28.910 --> 00:14:30.590
Back him up!

00:14:30.860 --> 00:14:31.860
Stop it!

00:14:31.860 --> 00:14:35.700
If we take another hit from that
 supersonic wave, we'll lose our lives, too!

00:14:36.010 --> 00:14:38.190
We have no choice 
but to trust Sensui with this!

00:14:38.860 --> 00:14:42.550
Damn! All we can do is watch?!

00:14:43.120 --> 00:14:44.370
Sensui!

00:14:45.350 --> 00:14:46.360
Huh?

00:14:46.360 --> 00:14:48.660
That man is waving his hands.

00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:55.120
Hey! Are you okay?!

00:14:55.450 --> 00:14:57.190
Hey, monk!

00:14:57.190 --> 00:14:59.790
Sorry, but can you do us a favor?!

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:03.630
I don't know what's going on, but gladly!

00:15:03.900 --> 00:15:07.250
Yoshinaga! Get a bit closer to him!

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:10.450
That's not an easy thing to ask.

00:15:10.450 --> 00:15:12.010
I'll do what I can.

00:15:12.010 --> 00:15:15.790
Hey! Over here!

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:19.490
Pull it as hard as you can toward you!

00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:24.480
I still don't know what's going on,
 but I'll do it!

00:15:30.110 --> 00:15:32.070
And there!

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:35.680
Huh?!

00:15:36.190 --> 00:15:38.040
Way to go, monk!

00:15:39.590 --> 00:15:42.540
Now! Everyone, jump out!

00:15:54.770 --> 00:15:57.230
Mother! Hold on tight!

00:15:57.560 --> 00:15:58.510
Hup!

00:16:04.800 --> 00:16:08.340
Oh, you're light!

00:16:08.340 --> 00:16:10.040
Are you hurt at all?

00:16:10.040 --> 00:16:11.800
Th-Thanks.

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:14.540
Hey! I'm going on ahead!

00:16:14.810 --> 00:16:16.020
Doctor, hurry up!

00:16:22.270 --> 00:16:23.220
Brian!

00:16:28.710 --> 00:16:30.130
Are you all right, Brian?!

00:16:32.590 --> 00:16:33.830
I'm fine.

00:16:35.020 --> 00:16:38.010
You saved us! Um, who are you?

00:16:38.010 --> 00:16:41.250
Me? I'm Onikura Yukinojyo!

00:16:41.250 --> 00:16:43.270
I'm a warrior monk from Honganji!

00:16:43.680 --> 00:16:47.100
Worry not, you're with me now!

00:16:47.580 --> 00:16:49.930
Thank you, Yukinojyo-san.

00:16:49.930 --> 00:16:51.230
You're strong.

00:16:55.260 --> 00:16:56.440
Where's Kenroku?!

00:16:58.730 --> 00:16:59.690
What now?!

00:17:05.840 --> 00:17:11.210
Your opponent is Sanada Kenroku!

00:17:14.620 --> 00:17:17.510
Even if I don't know how to steer this thing,

00:17:20.770 --> 00:17:25.310
it's easy enough to make it fall into you!

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:27.560
Kenroku?!

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:43.830
Kenroku!

00:17:53.440 --> 00:17:55.430
Hey!

00:17:59.910 --> 00:18:01.120
Kenroku!

00:18:04.340 --> 00:18:06.850
I'm not about to kick the bucket yet.

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:12.980
You have my thanks, Onikura-dono.

00:18:13.510 --> 00:18:14.980
Yeah.

00:18:15.870 --> 00:18:18.440
Stop it already, you two.

00:18:19.040 --> 00:18:22.280
You're both being too 
modest with each other.

00:18:22.280 --> 00:18:24.280
It's making me uncomfortable.

00:18:24.280 --> 00:18:25.620
That's right!

00:18:25.620 --> 00:18:29.000
We managed to survive 
because all of you fought for us!

00:18:29.320 --> 00:18:33.100
But without Onikura-dono,

00:18:33.100 --> 00:18:35.950
you might have been in danger, Kathleen.

00:18:36.550 --> 00:18:38.060
What now?

00:18:38.060 --> 00:18:41.050
It was all thanks to your efforts.

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:45.010
All of it was the guidance of the Buddha.

00:18:46.190 --> 00:18:47.760
Good grief.

00:18:52.830 --> 00:18:59.360
Still, I'm surprised to see 
the Onikura Yukinojyo of Honganji

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:02.280
who gave Oda Nobunaga such trouble.

00:19:02.780 --> 00:19:05.340
You've come here from 
a past further back than ours,

00:19:05.810 --> 00:19:10.130
so I guess you were transported 
here the same way.

00:19:10.700 --> 00:19:14.890
The enemy was in pursuit 
and just as I decided to end myself,

00:19:14.890 --> 00:19:18.040
I fell into a huge shaft.

00:19:18.040 --> 00:19:20.350
Next thing I knew, I was here.

00:19:20.350 --> 00:19:24.220
I thought this was the other world 
when I awoke, so I was stunned.

00:19:26.530 --> 00:19:29.200
Mother, what's Honganji?

00:19:29.970 --> 00:19:32.760
It was known as the Ishiyama-Honganji War,

00:19:32.760 --> 00:19:35.600
and it lasted ten years starting in 1570.

00:19:35.930 --> 00:19:39.740
The main base of the warrior monks 
who fought against Oda Nobunaga

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:42.800
was known as Ishiyama Honganji.

00:19:44.050 --> 00:19:47.370
Yukinojyo-san was one 
of the monks there, it seems.

00:19:50.960 --> 00:19:53.800
Apparently we finally 
have a lead on the vaccine.

00:19:53.800 --> 00:19:56.710
We just need to get it safely to Niigata.

00:19:57.480 --> 00:19:59.970
Are we spending the night here?

00:20:00.430 --> 00:20:04.470
Yeah, it's safer than trying 
to wander around with our cargo.

00:20:05.090 --> 00:20:07.340
I took a quick look around,

00:20:07.340 --> 00:20:10.830
but there doesn't seem 
to be any Gibia on this floor.

00:20:11.150 --> 00:20:14.730
Once night passes, we'll return to camp 
for a bit first thing in the morning.

00:20:16.440 --> 00:20:18.980
The moonlight filters in well here.

00:20:20.020 --> 00:20:23.240
Gibia shouldn't like 
places like this, either.

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:27.900
Still, what on earth was 
that thing we just fought?

00:20:27.900 --> 00:20:29.010
Indeed...

00:20:29.360 --> 00:20:33.700
That thing was far stronger 
than a normal Gibia.

00:20:34.140 --> 00:20:40.030
All we know right now is that thing 
is a Gibia known as Meteora.

00:20:40.030 --> 00:20:41.420
Meteora...

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:46.800
Well, either way, I, the great Kenroku, 
cast it down into a deep hole!

00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:48.670
You don't need to worry about it anymore!

00:20:49.990 --> 00:20:52.100
You should never stop being cautious.

00:20:52.420 --> 00:20:57.440
After all, that's a unique type 
that is able to act even in daylight.

00:20:58.090 --> 00:21:04.890
So, this Gibia Virus or whatnot 
is causing people to transform into monsters?

00:21:04.890 --> 00:21:09.270
What a cruel trial from the Buddha.

00:21:11.420 --> 00:21:15.300
I need to return to our camp 
and do something there,

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:20.480
but there might still be 
Gibia lurking there.

00:21:21.310 --> 00:21:23.880
We'll get everything ready to depart.

00:21:24.940 --> 00:21:28.510
I'll treat your leg 
while we're at it, too, Brian.

00:21:29.860 --> 00:21:34.230
In that case, let's go the mall nearby 
and look for some daily necessities.

00:21:34.550 --> 00:21:35.920
Nice idea!

00:21:35.920 --> 00:21:39.230
I bet you get cold wearing 
that outfit all the time, Sensui.

00:21:39.560 --> 00:21:42.700
Not to mention, it looks like Kenroku 
and Yukinojyo won't be waking for some time.

00:21:44.570 --> 00:21:46.660
That's a good idea for you all.

00:21:47.410 --> 00:21:51.740
Stay cautious and be careful 
until we meet back up again.

00:21:53.990 --> 00:21:55.250
Maeda-dono...

00:21:56.690 --> 00:21:58.680
Thank you.

00:22:05.670 --> 00:22:09.360
Brian, how is your leg feeling?

00:22:10.570 --> 00:22:12.120
I'll look at it now.

00:22:13.360 --> 00:22:15.680
Doctor, I'm sorry.

00:22:15.680 --> 00:22:17.140
Don't worry about it.

00:22:18.360 --> 00:22:20.000
This will hurt a little.

00:22:20.510 --> 00:22:21.420
Yes.

00:22:25.020 --> 00:22:28.610
The pain killers should kick in soon.

00:22:30.550 --> 00:22:33.270
One day, when this whole journey is over,

00:22:33.740 --> 00:22:38.710
I'd like to take you out to 
a nice restaurant in my hometown.

00:22:39.040 --> 00:22:42.640
I like fish more than meat.

00:23:07.400 --> 00:23:09.780
<b>"Danger Zone"</b>
